        "problem": "Find the value of the double sum\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{25}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{70}(3{a}_{ij}+4{b}_{ij})\n$$\n\ngiven that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{25}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{70}{a}_{ij}=50,\\,{\\sum }_{i=1}^{25}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{70}{b}_{ij}=55.\n$$",
        "worked_solution": "The sum and constant multiple rules for double summations state that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({a}_{ij}+{b}_{ij}) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{a}_{ij}+{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{b}_{ij}, \\\\ {\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}k{a}_{ij} & =k{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{a}_{ij}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying these rules to the given sum, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{25}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{70}(3{a}_{ij}+4{b}_{ij}) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{25}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{70}3{a}_{ij}+{\\sum }_{i=1}^{25}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{70}4{b}_{ij} \\\\  & =3{\\sum }_{i=1}^{25}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{70}{a}_{ij}+4{\\sum }_{i=1}^{25}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{70}{b}_{ij} \\\\  & =3\\cdot 50+4\\cdot 55 \\\\  & =150+220 \\\\  & =370.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
